node_modules/
runtime/
*.db
# P4 #78 / ADR-0009 RELEASE EVIDENCE -- why this is NOT the obvious `artifacts/`
# + `!artifacts/release/`: a directory pattern swallows its whole subtree and git
# will not descend into an excluded directory, so the naive pair leaves the
# manifest ignored (verified: `git add --dry-run` refuses it, and `check-ignore -v`
# even reports `.gitignore:8:artifacts/` as the matching pattern). Narrowing the
# exclusion to `artifacts/*` fixes that, but the re-inclusion must name the
# DIRECTORY before git will descend into it -- `!artifacts/release/**` alone does
# not work either. Scope stays narrow: every other content dir (acceptance/probe/
# reports/security) and any future one remains ignored, i.e. fail-closed.
# Rationale and the full pattern matrix: docs/ADR/ADR-0009-release-evidence-provenance.md
artifacts/*
!artifacts/release/
!artifacts/release/**

# RESOLVED 2026-09-26. The stopgap below used to hide the continuation-watchdog
# trio from `git status`, on the reasoning that the files were "NOT part of this
# release yet" and that an untracked file would dirty the worktree and fail the
# gate's provenance checks. The rule said: "If they turn out to be product code,
# this rule is wrong: delete it, do not widen it."
#
# They are product code. Keeping the pipeline alive across a terminated session
# is the whole point of the deliverable, and a watchdog that is not in version
# control is a watchdog that exists only on one machine -- so the rule is
# deleted, not widened. The files were removed from disk and re-authored under
# `scripts/` with the installed task name (JEV-JCC-Continuation-Watchdog), where
# the rest of the operator-facing PowerShell already lives, and they are tracked.
#
# The stopgap is recorded here rather than silently dropped because the same
# temptation will come back the next time a file appears mid-freeze: the answer
# is to decide whose file it is, not to hide it from `git status`.
# (was: tools/continuation-watchdog*.ps1)

# P4 / E-05..E-07 leg re-signing -- the gate's own decision carriers.
# The three leg verdicts and the gate result ARE the release decision. Kept out
# of version control, re-signing them is an in-place overwrite git cannot see:
# `git status` stays clean, P-01 passes, and every check that reads artifacts/
# keeps reading whatever was there before -- so E-07 passes precisely because
# the thing it checks is outside the repository.
#
# Getting four exact files out of `artifacts/*` took three measured attempts:
#   1. `!artifacts/acceptance/final_sre_go.json` alone  -> no effect. The
#      directory `artifacts/acceptance` is itself excluded by `artifacts/*` and
#      git does not descend into an excluded directory, so the negation inside
#      was never reached.
#   2. adding `!artifacts/acceptance/` -> works, but re-includes EVERY file in
#      the directory (~240 of them became untracked at once, dirtying the tree
#      for reasons unrelated to the product), because `artifacts/*` never
#      matched those paths in the first place -- a `*` cannot span `/`.
#   3. this form: re-include the directory, re-exclude its contents with
#      `artifacts/acceptance/**`, then negate the four back in. Last matching
#      pattern wins, so the four survive and every sibling stays ignored.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v` and `git status --porcelain -uall`.
# Registered as KD-0012; the reason it survived to P4 is that the gap was in the
# ignore rules, not in the gate.
!artifacts/acceptance/
artifacts/acceptance/**
!artifacts/acceptance/final_sre_go.json
!artifacts/acceptance/final_architecture_go.json
!artifacts/acceptance/final_security_go.json
!artifacts/acceptance/final_gate_result.json

# P5 / S-04 evidence: the Control UI's 8-screen proof, and the ONLY artifact the
# gate's S-04 check accepts. It was untracked while S-04 read it, which means the
# check passed on this machine and would have failed with MISSING on a clone --
# the verdict was reproducible here and nowhere else. Found by P-06, which now
# asserts the property for every gate input instead of relying on this list
# staying complete. Do not delete this line without reading P-06's docstring:
# the whole point of tracking it is that an untracked evidence file verifies
# exactly once, on the machine that produced it.
!artifacts/acceptance/control_ui_smoke.json
# FINAL-phase evidence, same rule: each of these is read to decide whether the
# platform runs, so each has to travel with the repository.
!artifacts/acceptance/CONTINUATION_INFRA_TEST.json
!artifacts/acceptance/DETACHED_SURVIVAL_TEST.json
!artifacts/acceptance/SURFACE_EVIDENCE.json
!artifacts/acceptance/WATCHDOG_RECOVERY_PROOF.json
!artifacts/acceptance/REBOOT_RECOVERY.json
!artifacts/acceptance/project_run_gate_result.json
# The soak's T1 proof, kept SEPARATE from WATCHDOG_RECOVERY_PROOF.json on purpose.
# Both producers used to write the same path, which meant FINAL-09 overwrote the
# exact bytes FINAL-08's record pointed at: the soak claimed a verdict about a file
# that no longer contained it. Two claims, two files.
!artifacts/acceptance/SOAK_WATCHDOG_PROOF.json
# FINAL-12 / stop-condition section L: the control-plane proofs. Each is written
# by the falsifier that measures the claim (tools/tests/interruption_recovery.py,
# watchdog_election_falsifier.py, runtime_lease_falsifier.py,
# provenance_integration.py) and READ by artifacts/acceptance/project_run_gate.py
# to decide the release. Same rule as the FINAL-phase evidence above: a proof read
# to decide whether the platform runs has to travel with the repository, or it
# verifies exactly once, on the machine that produced it.
!artifacts/acceptance/CONTROL_HEARTBEAT_PROOF.json
!artifacts/acceptance/INTERRUPTION_RECOVERY_PROOF.json
!artifacts/acceptance/WATCHDOG_ELECTION_PROOF.json
!artifacts/acceptance/RUNTIME_LEASE_PROOF.json
!artifacts/acceptance/PROVENANCE_INTEGRATION_PROOF.json
# The FINAL-12 (project-run) gate SCRIPT. It sat untracked while
# tools/jcc_continuation.py named it as a step's script and CONTROLLER_INFRA's
# suite ran its --selftest, which means a clone would have had a pipeline step
# pointing at a file that does not exist -- the same "verifies once, on the
# machine that produced it" defect the FINAL-phase evidence lines fix. Named
# individually, like its sibling final_gate_run.py; the ignore rule is not widened.
!artifacts/acceptance/project_run_gate.py
# NOT whitelisted, deliberately: artifacts/acceptance/gate_runs.jsonl. It records
# WHEN a gate ran and WHICH commit it saw -- an observation about a moment, not
# about the tree. A tracked file that changes on every run is the defect the
# gate's verdict was just cured of.
build/
dist/
*.log
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
credentials*
auth.json
.sandbox-secrets
id_rsa
id_ed25519
# Windows reserved device names accidentally created in the repo root (e.g. by a
# shell redirect such as `... > nul`). They are 0-byte shells -- NOT real files --
# but git still reports them as untracked, which makes `dirty == True` and fails
# the provenance checks (P-01/P-05). Ignore them; do not delete them (只搬不删).
nul
NUL

# v1.1 Real Jev Provider secrets and tokens (added 2026-09-27 by the
# v1.1 baseline commit on feature/jcc-v1.1-activation). The provider
# uses an env var (jev.api_key_env) and a base URL; the secret itself
# never enters the repository. These rules are belt-and-suspenders so
# an accidental drop of a recorded credential file is invisible to git
# and the gate's P-01 stays satisfiable.
fixtures/v1.1/**/*.api_key
fixtures/v1.1/**/*.tok
fixtures/v1.1/**/real_session_*.json

# Test scratch roots (added 2026-10-04, relay, after CR-004/relocation work).
#
# WHY THIS BLOCK IS A FREEZE GATE, NOT COSMETICS. `release_truth.py` treats ANY
# untracked path as PRODUCT, so a test run that drops a basetemp inside the
# checkout makes the worktree dirty and the freeze cannot be signed. That is
# fail-closed working as designed: the run genuinely left files where they do
# not belong. The fix belongs here rather than in the rule that judged it --
# loosening "untracked == dirty" to make a command turn green would let real
# contamination through.
#
# `packages/conftest.py` redirects JCC_SPOOL_DIR and JCC_STATE_DIR into the
# per-session temp dir, so a basetemp inside the repo also collects spool
# jsonl + temp config.toml -- not just empty directories.
#
# Patterns are anchored per-depth and cover the shapes actually observed:
#   * .relay_bt*   -- this agent's --basetemp dirs (21 of them accumulated)
#   * .pytest_bt*  -- the conventional name for the same trick
#   * jcc-spool*   -- a spool dir created in-tree if JCC_SPOOL_DIR is relative
#   * *.jcc-spool* -- the same under another name
# Relative (leading-slash-free) rules match at ANY depth, because pytest is
# invoked from packages/, from the repo root, and from ad-hoc subdirectories.
.relay_bt*/
.pytest_bt*/
.jcc_bt*/
**/jcc-spool*/
**/jcc_spool*/
**/*.jcc-spool/
# Codex observer state + agent-side hooks landing in-tree when their env
# overrides are set to a relative path.
**/codex_observer_state.json
**/jcc_execution_state.json
runtime/v1.1/**/shadow_endpoint.token

